@yusukebe Thank you!
I've been struggling with this.

I think `jsx` will be used in the old React import style, as shown below. I didn't add it because I didn't think it would be used in "hono/jsx/dom" usage.  I think "hono/jsx/dom" is only used with "jsxImportSource".

```ts
/* @jsx jsx */
import { jsx } from "hono/jsx/dom";
```

That said, `jsx` has been exported from 'hono/jsx' and I think you are right that it would be easier to understand if `jsx` was exported from “hono/jsx/dom" as well, as you pointed out.

What should we do, export it?

@usualoma 

I was wondering, but I think it should export `jsx`. Not many people may use `jsx`, but I may sometimes use `jsx` directly.

For example, in the case of HonoX, `jsx` is imported [here](https://github.com/honojs/honox/blob/a186c42bfd35c05954df614078e89fcb19c1263c/src/client/client.ts#L2C1-L2C56) from `hono/jsx/dom/jsx-runtime`, but `hono/jsx/dom` is better.

@usualoma 

Thanks for the explanation! Then, how about go with "exporting `jsx`"? One more reason is that `hono/jsx` is exporting `jsx`, so I want to make it the same as that.

If you agree, could you add that?

